The function is already minimal, so this is only a micro-optimization:

- It reads the `profile` pointer and `profileIndex` into locals once each.
- It marks the found-field path as the likely branch.

Every input returns the same value as before. Any speedup will be small at best.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    const auto* p = profile;
    const auto idx = profileIndex;
    if (__builtin_expect((p != NULL) && (idx < p->numFields), 1))
        return p->fields[idx].num;
    return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
}
```